  "raw_text": "A privacy architecture principle was enforced in the backup flow: a plaintext source must never be written to the backup directory. The `encrypt_it` source-removal step was rewired so that, before any plaintext is deleted, the source is first sealed with the user's SSH key via `seal_it`, the sealed ciphertext is archived to `~/backups`, and only the encrypted copy persists. Recovery is performed later with `unseal_it`, ensuring that what lands in backups is always opaque ciphertext that still round-trips faithfully to the original.",
